  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_001",
  "label": "The viewer is mapped onto the woman as the person who goes to see family for the barbecue",
  "description": "The text 'when you go see your family because of the barbecue' directly addresses the viewer ('you'), creating an analogical mapping where the viewer is projected onto the visual entity (the woman). The woman's angry, accusatory expression and pointing gesture serve as a visual representation of the viewer's internal frustration or annoyance at the situation described in the text. The mapping is established through the direct address ('you') in the text and the visual framing that makes the viewer feel personally targeted and blamed, as implied by the woman's expression and gesture.",
